e\u2011off:** C\u2019s communication difficulty, egocentric perception, and lack of willingness to pursue further education versus B\u2019s documented negative interpersonal behavior. The positive crew atmosphere for C suggests his teamwork is at least adequate, whereas B\u2019s interpersonal issues could directly undermine crew cohesion on long\u2011haul flights.\n**Remaining uncertainty:**\n- No explicit evidence of C\u2019s leadership ability or how his communication difficulty manifests in the cockpit.\n- No positive teamwork or communication data for B or D that could offset their interpersonal weaknesses.\n**What would change my vote:**\n- Concrete examples showing that B (or D) consistently works effectively with crew and that his negative remarks do not impair coordination.\n- Evidence that C\u2019s communication difficulties materially impair crew decision\u2011making or safety.\n- Any strong positive leadership or teamwork data for A or D that outweigh their current gaps.\nGiven the current balance of reliability, calmness under pressure, technical competence, and demonstrated positive crew interaction, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_1\", \"vote\": \"Candidate C\"}"}
